---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {chapterCollectionSources} from '../../lib/chapter-collection-sources.mjs';
import {chapterDocuments} from '../../lib/chapter-documents.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Map collections and source documents" description="Research routes into New Zealand historical maps, aerial photography, geological archives and environmental GIS.">
 <article class="page-wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Sources and collections</p><h1 class="page-title">Map collections and source documents</h1>
  <p>These collection notes accompany specific chapter paragraphs. They distinguish original records from later scans, repositories and web services. Sources checked on 11 October 2026.</p>
  <p>The University of Otago’s <a href="https://otago.libguides.com/c.php?g=171492&amp;p=7033025">GIS and datasets guide</a> provides a starting point for several of these research routes.</p>
  {chapterCollectionSources.map(source=><section id={source.id}><h2>{source.title}</h2><p>{source.text}</p><ul>{source.links.map(link=><li><a href={link.url}>{link.label}</a></li>)}</ul><p class="muted">{source.limitations}</p><p><a href={'/stories/'+source.articleSlug+'/#'+source.afterParagraphId}>Read the related paragraph in {source.articleTitle} →</a></p></section>)}
  <h2>Contributed documentary sources, 2007–2021</h2><p>Eight additional period documents, including national strategies, the 2007 Crown Forestry Rental Trust handout, GIS Day 2018, PLACE19 and 2021 publications, are catalogued with source-page findings, original identifiers and reuse status. <a href="/sources/documents/">Browse the contributed primary sources →</a></p>
  <h2>Download original documents</h2><ul>{chapterDocuments.map(document=><li><a href={document.assetPath} download>{document.title} (PDF, {(document.bytes/1000000).toFixed(1)} MB)</a> · <a href={'/documents/'+document.slug+'/'}>Document details</a></li>)}</ul>
 </article>
</Layout>
